Well... after literally hundreds of games started as a preist, I
finally playe done all the way through. I had solved it 5 or 6 times
before, but all with barbarians. Here, the only characters to have
ascened to demi-god(dess) hood were Barbarians, Valkeries, Samurai and
Wizards, so I am proud to be the first at our site to do it with a priest.

It took a lot of luck (and 8 wishes) to get the proper equipment. And I never
did get a scroll of charging... was lucky enough to get a wand of wishing in a
wand store on level 4 and then I got the one in the castle. Both had 3 charges
(plus the wand-turns-to-dust charge).

   Notable items:         Armor                       Amulets
                   +6 rust resistent Mjollnir        Life Saving
                   +3 shield of reflection
                   +5 gauntlets of dexterity            Rings 
                   +3 gray dragon scale mail         Protection +4
                   +5 helm of brilliance             Conflict
                   +3 Hawaian shirt
                   +3 cloak of protection

    I never found the speed boots, but I had the 1.3 intrinsic speed anyway.
The armor class was at -41 when I finished (made a few trips to my priestess
on level 10) and I had all the intriniscs, although I did not get my telepathy
until I had already started 'up' through hell (not one damn floating eye until
I created some with a cursed genocide).

    I didnt bother with the 'potion of paralysis on the wizard' technique
(assuming it still works...) I just killed him outright 4 times on the way 
up. Plus the automatic appearance on level one. I then made it through
the EndLevel without him appearing again...

    Only got a 1,009,562 for this game though... I was more interested in
having a priest solve it then get points...

    Oh well... back to your normal service.
